2.1

===================================
Version: 2.1
===================================

- updated with Total.js Flow 11.1: jComponent and the fix of dragging components
- sign in with OpenPlatform cloud (`sso` in the config): the groups and the teacher come from OpenPlatform, nobody can impersonate groups
- the students cannot read, edit or remove the code of the components, and they cannot import FlowStreams (they can duplicate their own); a FlowStream that a student exports or reads does not carry the code of the components
- every setting of the config can be given as an environment variable (FLOWEE_ plus the key in upper case), also the tokens of OpenPlatform; the docker-compose.yaml lists them
- activity log (Classroom): what each student does and when, with filters, download as CSV, retention in days (FLOWEE_ACTIVITY_DAYS) and a button to clear it
- forbidden components for each group (Classroom): they are taken out of the FlowStreams of the group; the ones that look like they reach files or the shell are marked and can be forbidden automatically
- observe in real time (Classroom): the teacher follows the editor of a student live, read only (the server refuses any change)
- exam mode (Classroom): the students of a group can work only between a start and an end, exporting and duplicating can be blocked while it is open, and the work is delivered by itself when it ends
- deliveries: the student delivers a FlowStream and the teacher gets a frozen copy with its date; the teacher opens it as a FlowStream, downloads it or downloads the last deliveries of a group to grade them
- limits for each student (Classroom): the number of FlowStreams that he can have, and the days without work before his FlowStreams are paused (he can resume them)
- palette of components for each group (Classroom): the teacher chooses the components that the FlowStreams of a group have, the students get them without being able to change their code
- a template of a group is only for the teachers: the students of the group do not see it
- the Docker image runs from the source: there are no bundles to maintain
- the image keeps its data in `/www/databases`, `/www/flowstream` and `/www/private`

